        "Charles L. Bennett",
        "David N. Spergel",
        "Lyman A. Page"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "WMAP's precise mapping of the cosmic microwave background made cosmology a precision science and established a remarkably successful standard model of the Universe.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Page led key experimental and instrumental work, while Spergel played a leading role in interpreting the cosmological results. The achievement depended on a broad mission team.",
        "maturity": "Independent measurements, especially Planck, have extensively confirmed the main cosmological picture.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundary between WMAP's specific contribution and the broader sequence of CMB experiments needs careful treatment."
        ]
      }
    },
