        "Charles H. Bennett",
        "Gilles Brassard",
        "Artur Ekert"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum key distribution helped establish quantum information as a physical field and showed how quantum principles can secure communication.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Brassard introduced the first influential protocol, and Ekert independently developed an entanglement-based approach. The distinct contributions are identifiable.",
        "maturity": "The principles are experimentally mature and have motivated extensive practical development, though secure operation depends on implementation details.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The credited names include two forms of Ekert's name; I use the uninitialled form exactly as listed."
        ]
      }
    },
