      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation offers a compelling account of early-universe dynamics and the origin of primordial structure, with major influence on modern cosmology.",
        "attribution": "Guth and Linde developed influential inflationary ideas, and Mukhanov made foundational contributions to the theory of primordial perturbations. The development involved multiple models and contributors.",
        "maturity": "The framework is mature theoretically, but the inflationary mechanism has not been established by a distinctive direct observation.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "There is no consensus on which inflationary model, if any, describes the early Universe.",
          "A definitive primordial gravitational-wave signal has not been observed."
        ]
      }
